# Sidebar

Responsive navigation with a sticky desktop rail and an accessible mobile drawer. Supports nested items, icons, badges and active-page tracking.

## App sidebar

Use `variant="app"` for compact application navigation with expandable branches. Enable `resizable` and `collapsible` to let users adjust or hide the rail.

<SidebarSandbox />

## Documentation tree

Use `branchBehavior="navigate"` to navigate and expand a parent in one click, with `treeLines` to connect nested items. The separate caret button expands or collapses a branch without navigating or closing the mobile drawer. Set `value` from the active route to reveal its branch automatically.

<DocsExample title="Documentation tree usage example" source={sidebarDocumentationSource} htmlSource={sidebarDocumentationHtmlSource}><SidebarDocumentationExample /></DocsExample>

## Classic sidebar

Use the optional `itemActions(item)` snippet for separate row actions such as adding a project chat or opening a rename/remove menu. Actions appear on row hover or keyboard focus and remain visible on touch devices. Keep chat state and action handlers in the consumer.

Set `variant="classic"` for a project or chat list. Use `--aesir-sidebar-item-padding` or `--aesir-sidebar-mobile-item-padding` to adjust item spacing.

Use the `itemLeading(item)` snippet to render custom leading content, such as an avatar with a presence indicator. It replaces the default icon or status dot in both the desktop rail and mobile drawer; item selection, badges, and keyboard behavior remain unchanged. Render the item's icon inside the snippet for entries that do not need custom content.

<DocsExample title="Sidebar usage example" source={sidebarExampleSource} htmlSource={sidebarExampleHtmlSource}><SidebarExample /></DocsExample>
